  "definition": "Flood mapping locates land affected by water or describes the probability, depth, velocity or consequences of flooding. The name covers several products with different meanings: an image-derived outline of an event, a forecast of what may happen, a modelled risk zone, or a planning scenario. A useful map therefore states its source, acquisition or valid time, spatial scale and intended decision.",
